* Q9K_MemTrace -- backend-neutral memory event fields.  The C event
* router writes these fields before calling the current output backend.
* $1650-$1663 belongs to F$VModul and $1664/$1668 to F$SetSys.
* $1690-$16B4 belongs to F$TLink.  Keep this block in the verified gap
* $16C0-$16F8, immediately before the memory-owner table at $1710.
Q9K_MemTraceEnabled       equ $16C0      * Q9_u32, 0=disabled, 1=enabled
Q9K_MemTraceOp            equ $16C4      * Q9_u32, 1=request, 2=return, 3=alloc, 4=free, 5=largest, 6=process release
Q9K_MemTraceRequest       equ $16C8      * Q9_u32, requested size
Q9K_MemTraceAddress       equ $16CC      * Q9_u32, allocated/returned address
Q9K_MemTraceSize          equ $16D0      * Q9_u32, granted/returned size
Q9K_MemTraceError         equ $16D4      * Q9_u32, error code or zero
Q9K_MemTraceHead          equ $16D8      * Q9_u32, free-list head after event
Q9K_MemTraceName          equ $16DC      * Q9_u32, current process module name
Q9K_MemTraceContextHdr    equ $16E0      * Q9_u32, temporary module context

